#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Capital Compass - local server

PRICE SOURCES, in order:
  1. BULK - one request returns a whole index of stocks. The server TRIES a
     list of candidate index names at startup and keeps whichever ones work,
     so a wrong guess no longer breaks everything. See /api/sources.
  2. SWEEP - every watchlist symbol not covered by a working bulk source is
     fetched individually, continuously, about one per second.
  3. ACTIVE - rows with a BUY note also get their own request each cycle,
     because IEP / IEQ / casStatus only appear in the per-symbol reply.

Standard library only - nothing to install.
"""

